# Renault Megane II five-door hatchback, 2002-2008.
#
# The second-generation Megane in its phase-1 form (2002-2006), on sale in
# Britain from the end of 2002 and replaced in 2008 by the Megane III. The
# five-door hatchback was the volume body; the three-door was marketed in
# Britain as the "Sport Hatch".
# https://www.renault.co.uk/ (Megane model page, cited in the reference pack)
#
# Dimensions 4.209 x 1.777 x 1.457 m, wheelbase 2.625 m. Source: the reference
# pack's notes. The hull measures 4.209 m on a 2.625 m wheelbase (62.4 per
# cent) and 1.777 m wide; mirrors take it to 1.927 m.
#
# Shape reference: no true side elevation exists. The model was built from a
# beige five-door seen about 30-35 degrees forward of side-on, a grey-green
# five-door from the front right and the same car from the rear left, with the
# wheel centres fixed by the published ratio. The signature is the long almost
# flat roof over a near-vertical tailgate.
#
# The first build sank all eight glazing panels inside the cabin and buried
# parts of the lamps; a bounded fix moved each pane to a measured 14-16 mm
# proud of the local body surface and re-seated the lamps, with no glazing
# intersecting the hull or cabin.
#
# Colours: no British-market names were established for the Megane II (no UK
# brochure was found), so the objects carry plain names: white, silver, black
# and red. Weights white 3, silver 3, red 2, black 2, total 10, provisional
# pending the central rebase.
#
# Speed 185 km/h, the 1.6-litre car's quoted maximum. Comfort 90/465, on the
# line 330 + 1.5 x 90: roomy and quiet for its class. Classes 0,1.
#
# Dates are road presence: late 2002 intro, retires staggered 2018-2021 on a
# sixteen- to nineteen-year tail.
#
# Metres master: citycars/4.5/renault-megane-ii.blend. Interchange:
# citycars/4.5/renault-megane-ii.dae (81 objects). References:
# citycars/references/renault-megane-ii/ (gitignored; Wikimedia Commons).
#
# Accepted deviations: the nose is faceted rather than the real car's rounded
# "flame" form, and the body is more slab-sided than the photographs. At 128 px
# the long flat roof and the near-vertical tailgate read as the Megane II.

obj=citycar
name=RenaultMeganeII(White)
copyright=JamesPetts

DistributionWeight=3
intro_year=2002
intro_month=12
retire_year=2021
retire_month=6
speed=185
class=0,1
maximum_comfortable_journey_minutes=90
maximum_tolerable_journey_minutes=465

